course: dictionary
lesson: 9961
title: Tax: money for shared things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tax is money that people and businesses must pay to the government. The government uses it for schools, roads, hospitals and police. «Council tax pays for local things like potholes and bins.» So tax is how everyone pays for things we share.
explain: Tax can also be a verb. To tax something means to make people pay tax on it. Tax can describe work too: «a taxing job» is a job that makes you tired. Check the sentence: is it about money, or about hard work?
explain: Tax has different names in different places. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, many prices include VAT or GST. In the USA and Canada, it is called sales tax. When you see a word you don't know, read the words around it, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Tax is money people and businesses pay to the government.
fact: «Tax relief» means a tax cut, so you pay less tax.
fact: Some taxes are taken from wages. This is called income tax.
fact: Sales tax is added at the till in some countries, so the total is more than the price on the label.
fact: «Taxing» can mean hard work that tires you out.
exercise: What does tax mean? | A kind of sweet | *Money people must pay to the government | A type of weather | Something you find in a park
exercise: «It was a taxing job, and she was worn out at the end.» What does taxing mean here? | Free money | Quick and easy | *Hard work that tires you out | Very cheap
exercise: «VAT is £2 of a £12 toy in the UK.» How much of the price is VAT? | £10 | *£2 | £12 | £1
test: «Tax relief» means a tax cut. What does tax relief mean? | Extra tax on sweets | Lost money | *A tax cut | Free school lunches
test: «£110 a month is 12 × £110 = £1,320 a year.» How much is £110 a month over a whole year? | *£1,320 | £1,100 | £1,220 | £132
exam: Which sentence uses tax as a verb, meaning to make people pay tax? | «She paid her tax by card.» | *«The government will tax sugary drinks.» | «The tax on the toy is £2.» | «Tax-free sweets are cheaper.»
